The RNS Montgomery design follows VROOM: Accelerating (Almost All)
Number-Theoretic Cryptography Using Vectorization and the Residue Number
System, by Simon Langowski, Kaiwen He, and Srinivas Devadas.

Reference implementation: VROOM, commit
013169524f701ec62f95048c427ccf9065da1abe.

The VROOM reference implementation's MIT license is reproduced in
LICENSE-VROOM. The Rust arithmetic, parameter generator, and SIMD kernels
in this crate are native implementations.

src/field/inverse.rs adapts binary-GCD batching and packed transformation
coefficients from blst 0.3.16.
